course: dictionary
lesson: 10344
title: Big words for big rules
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Transgression is a formal word, the kind you meet in religion, law and history. When you do not know a word like this, read the words around it, because they are its context and they leave clues. «I will confess my transgressions to the Lord.»
explain: To confess means to tell the truth about something you did wrong. So the speaker is telling God about their wrongs, and transgressions must mean wrongs or sins. Try your meaning in the sentence: «I will tell the truth about my wrongs to the Lord» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: In everyday talk, people say «breaking the rules», «doing wrong» or «a mistake». A transgression is the grown-up, formal way of saying it. In stories it can sound grand or old-fashioned: «he was forgiven for his transgressions».
fact: Transgression means an action that breaks a rule, law or moral code. It is a wrongdoing.
fact: In religion, a transgression is a sin.
fact: «A minor transgression» means a small wrong, and «forgive transgressions» means to pardon wrongs.
fact: In geology, transgression means the sea spreading over the land.
fact: You can talk about one transgression or many transgressions.
exercise: «A minor transgression» means what? | A long walk in the rain | A kind thank-you note | A large prize for winning a race | *A small wrong that breaks a rule
exercise: What does the speaker confess in «I will confess my transgressions to the Lord»? | Their lunch money | Their favourite food | *Their wrongs and sins | Their birthday wishes
exercise: Nadia says transgression is a silly word, just say mistake. Why might a writer choose transgression? | It is only used for weather reports | Nobody knows what it means | *It sounds more formal and can mean a wrong against a rule, law or moral code | It means a happy party with music
test: In religion, what is a transgression? | A school holiday | *A sin | A type of bread | A hymn sung at church
test: Which word is closest in meaning to transgression? | Breakfast | Balloon | Sunshine | *Wrongdoing
exam: Jayden says transgression only means the sea. Is he right? | Yes, because it sounds like ocean | No, it means a type of cloud | *No, it means a wrongdoing, and in geology it can mean the sea spreading over land | Yes, it only ever means the sea
